Karere #151 — detach the unused glib WorkSource under CEF's external message pump.

CEF's external_message_pump installs MessagePumpExternal, which inherits
base::MessagePumpForUI (== MessagePumpGlib on Linux). MessagePumpGlib's
constructor attaches a WorkSource to GTK's shared default GMainContext. With
an external pump, Chromium work is drained by the host's do_message_loop_work
(DirectRunWork), so that WorkSource is never dispatched — WorkSourcePrepare
keeps returning a 0 timeout and GTK's g_application_run busy-loops ppoll(0),
pinning one CPU core at 100% whenever Karere is idle/backgrounded.

This patch adds MessagePumpGlib::DetachWorkSource() and calls it from the
MessagePumpExternal constructor so the unused source is destroyed.

Apply from the Chromium src root: patch -p1 < karere-151-detach-worksource.patch

diff --git a/base/message_loop/message_pump_glib.cc b/base/message_loop/message_pump_glib.cc
index b7ff50ec9e..c00ee73223 100644
--- a/base/message_loop/message_pump_glib.cc
+++ b/base/message_loop/message_pump_glib.cc
@@ -510,6 +510,13 @@ MessagePumpGlib::~MessagePumpGlib() {
   owned_context_.reset();
 }

+void MessagePumpGlib::DetachWorkSource() {
+  if (work_source_) {
+    g_source_destroy(work_source_.get());
+    work_source_.reset();
+  }
+}
+
 MessagePumpGlib::FdWatchController::FdWatchController(const Location& location)
     : FdWatchControllerInterface(location) {}

